# Roo Code Rules — Angular 21 Project (legacy single-file shim)

Roo Code auto-loads `AGENTS.md` at the workspace root and any rules under
`.roo/rules/` (with per-mode rules under `.roo/rules-{mode}/`). Prefer those
locations for new rules; this single file is kept for backward compatibility.

All project rules are defined in `AGENTS.md` at the repository root.

Read and follow `AGENTS.md` for architecture, coding standards, component
patterns, banned patterns, and the Angular 18 → 21 migration playbook.

For detailed reference:
- `docs/PROJECT.md` — business domain
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — system design, signals, zoneless, hydration
- `docs/CONVENTIONS.md` — naming (v21 style guide), structure, testing
- `docs/TESTING.md` — Vitest setup, Karma migration
- `docs/MIGRATION_18_TO_21.md` — step-by-step upgrade path

Mode-specific guidance:
- `.roo/rules-code/` — implementation rules
- `.roo/rules-architect/` — planning rules
- `.roo/rules-ask/` — explanation rules
- `.roo/rules-debug/` — diagnostic rules
